Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

You are free to share and adapt the data for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit: cite the paper
"Repo-Blind Repair: Fixing Python Bugs Without Ever Seeing a Real Fix"
(McBride, 2026) and link to the repository. See CITATION.cff.

What the data is: 20,000 synthetic Python bug-fix records produced by
deterministic AST mutation of toy programs written for this task. No
real human bug fix, no teacher-model output, and no third-party code
was used in the corpus, so no third-party licence applies to it. The
provenance sidecar (source_index, operators, seed per record) lets
anyone regenerate every record byte-identically; see
data_generation/README.md.

